{% if revision | default(false) %}
This is a revision of the supplied previous_brief, not a new task. Incorporate the user's
answers and requested_changes into the scope, criteria, sources and scenarios where relevant.
Preserve unrelated agreed content. Remove a question only when its answer resolves the uncertainty.
Use review_history to preserve ALL earlier decisions, not just the last answer. The latest explicit
correction supersedes an earlier answer. Do not ask again about settled choices or introduce new
scope while revising. If the user delegates a decision to reasonable defaults, choose the simplest
reversible rule and state it in scope/criteria; do not ask the same question again.
Only genuine blocking contradictions justify a focused follow-up question (at most one).
Do not merely clear questions: the revised requirements and scenarios must reflect the answers.
The revision remains a draft for user review, not approval to execute.
{% endif %}
